    "result": "`search_products` is implemented in `solution.py`, and all 9 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't run a coverage measurement, so I can't confirm the 90% gate. The tests do exercise every branch of the function.\n\n- **Search:** it uses a parameterised SQLite `LIKE ... ESCAPE` query. That makes the match ASCII case-insensitive and treats `%`, `_` and `\\` in `name_contains` as plain characters.\n- **Ordering and validation:** `order_by` is limited to `name` or `price`, with ties broken by `id` ascending. `limit` and `offset` must be real integers in range (booleans are rejected), otherwise it raises `ValueError`.\n- **Tests:** they cover the stock filter, the result keys, case-insensitive matching, literal wildcards, `max_price`, ordering and ties, and `limit` and `offset`. They also cover invalid arguments and that the database isn't modified.\n\nOne assertion in `test_substring_case_insensitive` is weak. Its first line ends in `or True`, so it can never fail. The second assertion in that test does check the result, but you may want to delete the first line.",
